              Now for each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_J(-|y)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_F(-|y)
              are just
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+measures"} probability measures
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kolmogorov"}
              applies. We only need to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_J
              is measurable in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              if and only if the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_F
              are. Now if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_J
              is measurable, so is
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_F
              = succeed "." do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  pi-system
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/pi-system"} ?
          %h3#in_terms_of_the_giry_monad In terms of the Giry monad
          %p
            The result in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+kernels"} Markov kernels
            can be restated in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            as follows.
          %p
            Once again, recall that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi J
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_J,\mathcal{A}_J)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiltered+limit"} cofiltered limit
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meas"} Meas
            of the diagram formed by the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_F,\mathcal{A}_F)
            and their projections.
          %p
            Now, if the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_j
            are
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel"} standard Borel
          %p
          #kolmogorov_giry.num_cor
            %h6 Corollary
            %p The Giry monad preserves this limit.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              We have to show that given a measurable space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+functions"} measurable functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi J
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_J:Y\to X_J
              and families of measurable functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_F:Y\to X_F
              such that for each inclusion
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ⊆
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\subseteq G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Meas"} Meas
              commutes.
