              Now since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stoch"} Stoch
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kleisli+category"} Kleisli category
              of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giry+monad"} Giry monad
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Stoch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi Meas
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi PX
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Stoch(Y,X) \cong Meas(Y,PX)
            %p
              natural in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#kolmogorov_kernels"}
          %h2#in_markov_categories In Markov categories
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+categories"} Markov categories
            the Kolmogorov extension theorem appears in the form of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiom
            that the category can satisfy, an abstraction of the universal property in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+Markov+kernels"} category of Markov kernels
            given above.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a Markov category, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_j)_{j\in J}
              be a family of objects. A
              %strong Kolmogorov product
              of them is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+tensor+product"} infinite tensor product
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ⨂
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X_J=\bigotimes_{j\in J} X_j
            %p
              such that all finite projections (marginalizations)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi J
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_J\to X_F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\subseteq J
              finite, are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Markov+category#deterministic_morphisms"} deterministic morphisms
          %p
            The category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BorelStoch"} BorelStoch
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel+spaces"} standard Borel spaces
          %p
